{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"83c58528174d4b31","type":"text","text":"[story concept]\n\nPEDRO AND THE BURRO\n\nWell, anyway, uh, a long time ago, down in Mexico, up in the hill towns, there lived a lot of poor families, but they were very, very happy. And there was one family especially, and the son was named Pedro. And he lived with his father and mother. And his pet was not a cat, not a dog, not a parrot or anything like that, but it was a little donkey, okay, and it was actually a burro.\n\nSo, anyway, they used to go out and they'd play around in the field. And he'd brush the burro and wipe his eyes out and feed him. And the burro would snuggle up against him when they had a nap. And everything was wonderful. And they did go to school. And the burro would follow Pedro and his friends to the school.\n\nAnd naturally, it was a little one room schoolhouse. So everybody knew Pedro and everybody knew the burro. And the burro could not come inside, because after all they didn't allow animals. So what happened? There was a big shady tree outside the classroom, and the burro used to stand under there with a bucket of water, or sometimes lay down, or sometimes walk around, and wait for the children to get out of class.\n\nNow, the teacher had a tough time because a lot of times the children were all looking out the window yelling at the burro to come so they could pet him. But what happened at the end of the day, all the kids would come out and the burro would be so happy and kick up his heels and walk over to all the students to pet him and then he'd walk home with Pedro.\n\nNow, this would happen every day and it was wonderful for the children and wonderful for the school and all of the families, okay. So, and Pedro would get home and eat his dinner and after dinner he'd put the burro in the barn. And brush him down, feed him, wipe his eyes, and, and give him a hug goodnight.\n\nSo this went on and on, it was a wonderful life, and it really helped the little town. But one day, when Pedro had the burro at school, and they all came out after class, and you know what? There was no burro. The burro was gone. And the class, including the teacher, looked all over for the burro. And they couldn't find the burro anywhere.\n\nAnd they all started crying, even the teacher. So they looked and looked, and Pedro came home to his parents, and he's crying, and his parents said, well let's go see the policeman. So they went to see the policeman. And they told him the story and he said, don't worry, Pedro. This is a small village and I will find your burro.\n\nAnd he's still crying. He couldn't help him. So the next day, after school, the policeman came by Pedro's home and said, I found the burro. Come on with me. So they all came and they walked through the forest. Sort of a beaten down path. And they came to this rickety little old, little old house, if you want to call it that.\n\nAnd there's the old man sitting outside, petting a burro. He's got a rope on him, and the burro was snuggling up with him and everything. And the man got up and said, I'm sorry I stole your burro, but I was so lonely and I need something for affection and I love the burro. And he gave him a hug, but here you have the burro back.\n\nAnd the policeman said, okay, give the burro back to Pedro. Now, Pedro took the burro home, but he felt so bad. And he told his parents the story, and of course they were with him too, but he said, what are we going to do? So every few days, they would pack up a little lunch, and they would go over to the old man's house and let him play with the burro.\n\nAnd a few times, they invited the man to come to their house to see the burro and have dinner with them. So this went on and on. Pedro went to school. He went to visit the old man, and played with the burro, and everything ended just beautifully.\n","x":-1553,"y":-1360,"width":696,"height":840},
		{"id":"58216a2288ca3b9f","type":"text","text":"[tone]\nHeartwarming, compassionate, and uplifting","x":-497,"y":-1360,"width":180,"height":117},
		{"id":"817fbfb0b08ff4ff","type":"text","text":"[theme]\nThe power of compassion, understanding, and friendship","x":-685,"y":-940,"width":250,"height":153},
		{"id":"1460543f307950b1","type":"text","text":"**Story Outline: Pedro and the Burro**\n\n**Part 1: A Simple Life in the Hills**\n- **Scene 1:** Introduction to Pedro, his loving family, and their pet burro. They live in a small, happy village in the hills of Mexico.\n- **Scene 2:** Pedro's daily routine with the burro: playing in the fields, grooming, and napping together.\n- **Scene 3:** The burro follows Pedro and his friends to school, waiting under a shady tree outside the classroom.\n\n**Part 2: School Days and Friendships**\n- **Scene 1:** The children are distracted during class, excitedly looking out the window at the burro.\n- **Scene 2:** At the end of the school day, the children rush out to pet the burro, who joyfully greets them.\n- **Scene 3:** Pedro and the burro walk home together, where Pedro cares for the burro before bedtime.\n\n**Part 3: The Unexpected Disappearance**\n- **Scene 1:** One day, after school, Pedro and his friends discover that the burro is missing.\n- **Scene 2:** The entire class, including the teacher, searches for the burro but can't find him.\n- **Scene 3:** Pedro returns home in tears, and his parents suggest going to the policeman for help.\n\n**Part 4: The Search for the Burro**\n- **Scene 1:** The policeman reassures Pedro and promises to find the burro.\n- **Scene 2:** The next day, the policeman arrives at Pedro's home with news of having found the burro.\n- **Scene 3:** Pedro and his parents follow the policeman through the forest to a rickety old house.\n\n**Part 5: A Lonely Old Man**\n- **Scene 1:** They find an old man sitting outside the house, petting the burro, who is snuggling up to him.\n- **Scene 2:** The old man tearfully explains that he took the burro because he was lonely and needed affection.\n- **Scene 3:** The policeman asks the old man to return the burro to Pedro, and the old man reluctantly agrees.\n\n**Part 6: Compassion and Understanding**\n- **Scene 1:** Pedro and his parents feel sympathy for the lonely old man and discuss how to help him.\n- **Scene 2:** They decide to visit the old man regularly, bringing lunch and letting him spend time with the burro.\n- **Scene 3:** The old man is invited to their home for dinner and to play with the burro, forging a new friendship.\n\n**Part 7: A Happy Resolution**\n- **Scene 1:** Pedro continues his routine of school and caring for the burro, but now with added visits to the old man.\n- **Scene 2:** The old man's loneliness diminishes as he becomes part of Pedro's extended family, enjoying their company and the burro's affection.\n- **Scene 3:** The village, now united by compassion and understanding, celebrates the power of friendship and the joy it brings to everyone's lives.","x":-2073,"y":501,"width":1040,"height":1872,"color":"6"},
